                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "will: decisions, offers and predictions",
                    "explanation": "Will ('ll) + verbo en forma base se usa para:\n• decisiones que tomamos en el momento: I'll go and ask.\n• ofrecimientos: I'll pay for the coffees.\n• promesas: I won't forget the tickets again!\n• predicciones u opiniones sobre el futuro: I think it will be busy.\n\nNegativa: won't (will not). Pregunta: Will it be busy?\n\nCompáralo con be going to, que expresa un plan ya decidido: I'm going to book the tickets tonight (lo pensé antes) / I'll pay (lo decido ahora).",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Uso",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Decisión en el momento",
                          "I'll go and ask at the ticket office."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Ofrecimiento",
                          "I'll pay for the coffees."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Promesa",
                          "I won't forget the tickets again!"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Predicción",
                          "I think it will be quite busy."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Negativa",
                          "We won't find three seats together."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Pregunta",
                          "Will it be busy?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Plan decidido (going to)",
                          "I'm going to book the tickets tonight."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "Don't panic. I'll go and ask.",
                      "It will cost ten pounds each.",
                      "I'll pay. It was my mistake.",
                      "We won't find three seats together."
                    ]
                  }
                },
